# Held environment vs a panning projection window, with padding

## A. Colour + depth translate rigidly under a window offset
padding = 24 px each side; padded target 304x240
  window offset -24 px -> composite differs from a native render by 0 px
  window offset -16 px -> composite differs from a native render by 0 px
  window offset  -8 px -> composite differs from a native render by 0 px
  window offset  -1 px -> composite differs from a native render by 0 px
  window offset  +0 px -> composite differs from a native render by 0 px
  window offset  +1 px -> composite differs from a native render by 0 px
  window offset  +8 px -> composite differs from a native render by 0 px
  window offset +16 px -> composite differs from a native render by 0 px
  window offset +24 px -> composite differs from a native render by 0 px
worst difference across the pan: 0 px

## B. Negative control: crop at the WRONG offset
  crop off by  1 px -> 1468 px differ (proves the comparison is not blind)
  crop off by  4 px -> 5248 px differ (proves the comparison is not blind)
  crop off by 16 px -> 14128 px differ (proves the comparison is not blind)

## C. Occlusion is preserved, not merely colour
  actor at world x = -1.6 -> 0 px differ
  actor at world x = -0.8 -> 0 px differ
  actor at world x = +0.0 -> 0 px differ
  actor at world x = +0.8 -> 0 px differ
  actor at world x = +1.6 -> 0 px differ
worst difference with the actor crossing the occluder: 0 px

## D. The dither/quantisation anchor is NOT crop-invariant
  ditherLevels=8, window offset  +1 px -> 29560 px differ
  ditherLevels=8, window offset  +8 px -> 0 px differ
  ditherLevels=8, window offset +16 px -> 0 px differ
worst dither-anchored difference: 29560 px
(non-zero => a padded hold must also carry its dither/quantisation
 origin, or the retro pattern crawls against the panning window)
